Z||000002||sqoach||07-17-2001||01:01 PM||||Behind the seat works good<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/amp_install_1.JPG"> <P>Hey Tweek, don't you worry about your amp getting too hot in there and not getting any ventilation?<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumsig.JPG">      <BR>84 SE (FOR SALE)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)(take it off my hands for $50)<BR>86 SC (FOR SALE sometime in this summer)<BR>86 SE V6 (new project)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||07-17-2001||01:26 PM||||I have mine behind the seat. I just lifted the carpeting and put a piece of 1/2" plywood down, Then put the carpeting back. Mount the amp to the back with screws long enough to get into the wood. There is no need to glue or mount the wood since the carpet is sandwiched between the amp and the wood.<P>Before wiring was completed:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Setup_4.jpg">  <P>With cover installed:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/amprak_1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||07-17-2001||03:17 PM||||I have mine behind passenger seat also. You could see it here: <A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/alexft/Alex4mula/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://community-2.webtv.net/alexft/Alex4mula/index.html</A> <P>Very neat setup Orief  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red & White (:<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||onfire||07-17-2001||03:52 PM||||Alex4mula, How's the Vette coming along? Oh and to keep this on topic. I mounted mine behind the seat, sorry no pics.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tom88gt||07-17-2001||05:32 PM||||I have a small amp tucked under the AC/heater box in the passenger footwell.  I used a piece of sheet metal to fabricate a mounting board that fits under the heated box.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Alex4mula||07-18-2001||12:12 PM||||Onfire; The Vette is running perfectly. Just need to replace the seats and is ready to sell.<BR>Other option for a small amp is where the stock sub amp goes. Once they installed there a big alarm module in my car. But then not too much air circulation.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red & White (:<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||btoth||07-18-2001||12:54 PM||||I installed mine behind the passenger seat as well.  (Well, I wouldn't call it an <I>install</I>, it's just kinda laying there.)  I ran my power wire to the battery through the center console (there are some rubber plugs by the computer that i pulled the wire through) and ran the other wires under the console.  Nothing permanent and the amp doesn't move (or get hot) with the seat back.||||reg||1
